219
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:09,108
TOK-001 · Interview question

220
00:13:10,232 --> 00:13:11,880
Why can't this button be themed,

221
00:13:11,880 --> 00:13:14,076
and what token structure would you put in

222
00:13:14,076 --> 00:13:14,351
place?

223
00:13:14,351 --> 00:13:16,822
Then tell me how product teams should customise it,

224
00:13:16,822 --> 00:13:19,019
and what is wrong with the focus style.

225
00:13:25,669 --> 00:13:27,184
TOK-001 · 1.

226
00:13:27,184 --> 00:13:30,215
Raw values bypass the token system

227
00:13:31,340 --> 00:13:34,353
#0b5fff, white, 8px 16px, 4px and the font

228
00:13:34,353 --> 00:13:36,990
shorthand are written directly into the component.

229
00:13:36,990 --> 00:13:41,511
A theme can only change custom properties, so these values never change.

230
00:13:41,511 --> 00:13:45,655
Each one is also a copy of a decision made elsewhere,

231
00:13:45,655 --> 00:13:49,798
which drifts silently the next time the design team adjusts it.

232
00:13:51,174 --> 00:13:52,598
TOK-001 · 2.

233
00:13:52,598 --> 00:13:56,398
Components use palette tokens, which have no meaning

234
00:13:57,524 --> 00:14:00,136
--color-blue-700 names a colour, not a purpose.

235
00:14:00,136 --> 00:14:02,748
A dark theme cannot sensibly redefine "blue-700",

236
00:14:02,748 --> 00:14:06,107
and the acquired brand's primary colour is not blue

237
00:14:06,107 --> 00:14:06,854
at all.

238
00:14:06,854 --> 00:14:09,839
Themes need something to remap that describes intent.

239
00:14:09,839 --> 00:14:12,079
The usual answer is three layers:

240
00:14:13,453 --> 00:14:15,324
TOK-001 · 2.

241
00:14:15,324 --> 00:14:22,181
Components use palette tokens, which have no meaning · comparison 1

242
00:14:23,306 --> 00:14:24,845
Layer: Primitive (palette).

243
00:14:24,845 --> 00:14:26,385
Example: --ui-palette-blue-500: #0b5fff.

244
00:14:26,385 --> 00:14:29,979
Who uses it: Only the semantic layer.

245
00:14:31,354 --> 00:14:33,313
TOK-001 · 2.

246
00:14:33,313 --> 00:14:40,499
Components use palette tokens, which have no meaning · comparison 2

247
00:14:41,624 --> 00:14:42,699
Layer: Semantic.

