456
00:27:18,254 --> 00:27:20,535
TOK-002 · Follow-up 1

457
00:27:21,661 --> 00:27:24,615
A team says "just use !important in your fallback".

458
00:27:24,615 --> 00:27:25,927
Why is that worse?

459
00:27:31,378 --> 00:27:34,719
Important changes cascade priority; it does not repair the fallback

460
00:27:34,719 --> 00:27:37,726
order or a default declared on the wrong element.

461
00:27:37,726 --> 00:27:41,736
Inherited values still do not compete as direct declarations on the child.

462
00:27:41,736 --> 00:27:44,743
Escalating specificity makes scoped themes harder to override and

463
00:27:44,743 --> 00:27:47,750
creates an arms race between library and product CSS.

464
00:27:47,750 --> 00:27:51,759
Keep consumer override properties unset until supplied, consume the new name then

465
00:27:51,759 --> 00:27:55,435
the old name, and test the computed result at the component.

466
00:27:55,435 --> 00:27:59,779
The fallback is an expression, not a place to insert an important flag.

467
00:28:01,154 --> 00:28:03,651
TOK-002 · Follow-up 2

468
00:28:04,776 --> 00:28:09,979
How long should a deprecation period be for a library used by forty teams?

469
00:28:09,979 --> 00:28:13,696
What evidence would you collect before removing the old token?

470
00:28:18,851 --> 00:28:22,461
Choose a published window long enough for the slowest supported

471
00:28:22,461 --> 00:28:26,071
release cadence, with a removal major and named migration owners.

472
00:28:26,071 --> 00:28:28,237
For forty teams, collect repository scans,

473
00:28:28,237 --> 00:28:30,764
actual theme override uses, CI build results,

474
00:28:30,764 --> 00:28:31,847
and completion confirmations.

475
00:28:31,847 --> 00:28:33,653
Include applications that upgrade infrequently.

476
00:28:33,653 --> 00:28:36,902
Supply a codemod or guidance and track unresolved cases.

477
00:28:36,902 --> 00:28:40,873
Time elapsed alone is weak evidence: remove the old token when

478
00:28:40,873 --> 00:28:44,844
the policy permits it and consumers have a viable migration path,

479
00:28:44,844 --> 00:28:48,094
not merely when the library stopped referring to it.

480
00:28:49,469 --> 00:28:51,877
TOK-002 · Follow-up 3

481
00:28:53,002 --> 00:28:55,871
Could registering the property with @property help here?

482
00:28:55,871 --> 00:28:58,024
What would inherits need to be?

483
00:29:03,333 --> 00:29:06,428
Property registration can describe syntax and an initial value,

484
00:29:06,428 --> 00:29:10,211
but it cannot fix an incorrect cascade or decide which deprecated

485
00:29:10,211 --> 00:29:10,899
name wins.

486
00:29:10,899 --> 00:29:13,994
For a token intended to flow from theme containers

487
00:29:13,994 --> 00:29:16,745
into descendants, inherits normally needs to be true.

488
00:29:16,745 --> 00:29:20,184
A registered initial value can also make a variable present

489
00:29:20,184 --> 00:29:23,279
when it used to be missing, changing fallback behavior.

490
00:29:23,279 --> 00:29:24,999
Test that interaction before registration.

491
00:29:24,999 --> 00:29:28,094
Use registration when its typing or animation behavior is

492
00:29:28,094 --> 00:29:31,190
needed, not as a substitute for a compatibility chain.

