TOK-003 · What a strong candidate also mentions

611
00:37:23,326 --> 00:37:25,779
Contrast is a property of token pairs.

612
00:37:25,779 --> 00:37:28,232
Define tokens as pairs (surface and on-surface,

613
00:37:28,232 --> 00:37:31,737
selected and on-selected) and test every pair in every theme

614
00:37:31,737 --> 00:37:35,242
for 4.5:1 text contrast in CI, rather than checking components

615
00:37:35,242 --> 00:37:36,293
one by one.

616
00:37:36,293 --> 00:37:39,798
Themes can apply to a region, not just the page.

617
00:37:39,798 --> 00:37:44,705
Because tokens are custom properties, a data-ui-theme attribute on any element can work if

618
00:37:44,705 --> 00:37:49,261
the library supports it, but color-scheme must be set on that element too.

619
00:37:50,637 --> 00:37:53,111
TOK-003 · Follow-up 1

620
00:37:54,236 --> 00:37:55,774
Which browsers support light-dark()?

621
00:37:55,774 --> 00:38:00,004
What is your fallback for applications that must support older ones?

622
00:38:05,413 --> 00:38:10,008
Check the maintained support tables for the browser versions your applications actually support.

623
00:38:10,008 --> 00:38:14,249
The function is available in modern engines, but older supported versions may

624
00:38:14,249 --> 00:38:18,138
need light defaults, a prefers-color-scheme media query, and explicit attribute overrides.

625
00:38:18,138 --> 00:38:20,612
Use feature detection with supports where appropriate.

626
00:38:20,612 --> 00:38:24,500
Keep semantic token names identical across the modern and fallback implementations.

627
00:38:24,500 --> 00:38:27,681
The lesson links the support reference instead of freezing

628
00:38:27,681 --> 00:38:30,863
a list of browser versions that will become stale.

629
00:38:32,238 --> 00:38:34,908
TOK-003 · Follow-up 2

630
00:38:36,034 --> 00:38:40,093
