632
00:38:49,186 --> 00:38:52,621
markers, focus outlines, disabled states, and computed system colors.

633
00:38:52,621 --> 00:38:55,674
Capture representative screenshots with stable fonts and data.

634
00:38:55,674 --> 00:38:58,727
Assert the selected state is conveyed by a

635
00:38:58,727 --> 00:39:01,780
non-color cue and that keyboard focus remains visible.

636
00:39:01,780 --> 00:39:06,360
Emulation covers the browser's forced-color mode, not every operating-system palette or screen

637
00:39:06,360 --> 00:39:10,940
reader; retain manual checks on supported real configurations and document that limitation.

638
00:39:12,315 --> 00:39:14,969
TOK-003 · Follow-up 3

639
00:39:16,094 --> 00:39:19,668
A product team wants a third "high contrast" theme.

640
00:39:19,668 --> 00:39:22,845
What does your token structure need for that

641
00:39:22,845 --> 00:39:26,022
to be a remapping rather than a fork?

642
00:39:31,094 --> 00:39:34,605
Add another semantic mapping rather than duplicating component CSS.

643
00:39:34,605 --> 00:39:38,896
Components continue to consume surface, foreground, action, border, and focus roles.

644
00:39:38,896 --> 00:39:44,356
Define the high contrast mapping centrally, including interaction states, and verify paired contrast values.

645
00:39:44,356 --> 00:39:49,427
Scope the mapping so the application can choose it without replacing unrelated classes.

646
00:39:49,427 --> 00:39:52,938
Distinguish an authored high contrast theme from the user's

647
00:39:52,938 --> 00:39:56,058
forced-colors mode, which can still override author colors.

648
00:39:56,058 --> 00:39:58,398
Test the interaction of both choices.

