733
00:45:27,781 --> 00:45:30,143
layouts may use a distinct spacing contract.

734
00:45:30,143 --> 00:45:32,843
Explain which values follow font preferences and check

735
00:45:32,843 --> 00:45:35,543
that growing padding does not create avoidable overflow.

736
00:45:35,543 --> 00:45:39,255
With a larger root font, rem-based text and spacing both grow,

737
00:45:39,255 --> 00:45:42,967
so controls need flexible minimum dimensions rather than a fixed height.

738
00:45:44,343 --> 00:45:47,094
TOK-004 · Follow-up 2

739
00:45:48,219 --> 00:45:51,149
How would you automate the text-spacing check?

740
00:45:56,493 --> 00:46:00,981
Apply the WCAG text-spacing values to a representative rendered fixture: line

741
00:46:00,981 --> 00:46:04,245
height one point five, paragraph spacing two em,

742
00:46:04,245 --> 00:46:08,734
letter spacing point one two em, and word spacing point one

743
00:46:08,734 --> 00:46:09,550
six em.

744
00:46:09,550 --> 00:46:12,406
Verify text remains visible, labels can wrap,

745
00:46:12,406 --> 00:46:16,078
operations remain available, and containers do not clip essential

746
00:46:16,078 --> 00:46:16,486
content.

747
00:46:16,486 --> 00:46:19,343
Inspect geometry and screenshots, including long translations.

748
00:46:19,343 --> 00:46:22,607
Do not simply assert a stylesheet contains rem;

749
00:46:22,607 --> 00:46:25,463
the criterion concerns the resulting usable page.

750
00:46:25,463 --> 00:46:28,728
Combine this with separate text-resize and zoom checks.

751
00:46:30,103 --> 00:46:32,723
TOK-004 · Follow-up 3

752
00:46:33,848 --> 00:46:36,505
A dense data grid needs 24px rows.

753
00:46:36,505 --> 00:46:39,162
How do you meet target-size requirements there?

754
00:46:44,612 --> 00:46:46,859
Measure the actual targets and spacing.

755
00:46:46,859 --> 00:46:51,727
A twenty-four-pixel row height does not guarantee a twenty-four by twenty-four clickable area.

756
00:46:51,727 --> 00:46:55,472
Make the control's target large enough or meet the criterion's

757
00:46:55,472 --> 00:46:59,217
specific spacing exception, considering neighboring targets and overlapping hit areas.

758
00:46:59,217 --> 00:47:01,839
Keep small visual icons inside larger targets.

759
00:47:01,839 --> 00:47:04,460
If the design depends on another exception,

760
00:47:04,460 --> 00:47:07,831
document why it applies rather than treating density as

761
00:47:07,831 --> 00:47:08,580
an exemption.

762
00:47:08,580 --> 00:47:11,950
Test pointer use, keyboard operation, and text growth together.

763
00:47:13,326 --> 00:47:14,491
Final review checklist

764
00:47:15,616 --> 00:47:19,886
Review the lesson by answering each main question and follow-up aloud.

765
00:47:19,886 --> 00:47:22,992
For Design Tokens: Themes, Accessibility, and Public Contracts,

766
00:47:22,992 --> 00:47:25,710
connect each reported symptom to its mechanism,

767
00:47:25,710 --> 00:47:29,593
explain the corrected public contract, and name a regression check

768
00:47:29,593 --> 00:47:31,534
that exercises the consumer path.

769
00:47:31,534 --> 00:47:33,864
State compatibility and accessibility limitations clearly.

770
00:47:33,864 --> 00:47:36,581
The linked transcript, complete code, source questions,

771
00:47:36,581 --> 00:47:40,464
and verification report let you repeat the exercises at your

772
00:47:40,464 --> 00:47:41,241
own pace.

773
00:47:42,282 --> 00:47:44,611
That's the end of lesson 2.

